<title>JAPAN: MOF says to hold T-bill auction on Wednesday.</title>
<headline>MOF says to hold T-bill auction on Wednesday.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Ministry of Finance (MOF) will offer Treasury bills (T-bills) through a price competitive auction on Wednesday, a MOF official said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The T-bills to be offered through the auction are expected to have six-month maturities, and the size of the offer is expected to to be about 1.5 trillion yen, as 1.5 trillion yen worth of six-month Treasury bills is due on January 13, traders said.</p>
</text>
